{
  "slug": "revenuecat",
  "name": "Revenuecat",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Configure RevenueCat projects, apps, products, entitlements, and offerings directly from Claude Code. Manage your in-app purchase backend without leaving your development workflow.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **18 skills** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (18): `create-revenuecat-project` (Set up a complete RevenueCat project from scratch — creates apps, products, entitlements, offerings, and packages in the…), `integrate-revenuecat` (End-to-end RevenueCat integration — sets up the dashboard side via the RevenueCat MCP or the `rc` CLI (project,…), `revenuecat` (Used for all interaction with RevenueCat not covered by a different skill), `revenuecat-charts` (Use when the user asks about RevenueCat data, analytics, charts, or KPIs — querying charts with get-chart-options-schema and…), `revenuecat-cli` (Drive RevenueCat from the terminal with the `rc` CLI, an alternative to the RevenueCat MCP server for humans,…), `revenuecat-customer-center` (Add the RevenueCat Customer Center (self service subscription management UI) to an app), `revenuecat-entitlements-gate` (Check whether a RevenueCat user currently has access to a paid feature via entitlements), `revenuecat-experiment-analysis` (Use when the user asks to analyze or understand a RevenueCat experiment or its results), and 10 more\n- **MCP servers** (1): `RevenueCat`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install revenuecat@claude-plugins-official` from `RevenueCat/rc-claude-code-plugin`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 18,
    "mcp": 1
  },
